# Block web access to the git metadata directory.
#
# A ZIP install has no .git folder, so this used to be moot. Converting a ZIP
# install to a git clone (docs/SWITCH-FROM-ZIP-TO-GIT.md) creates one INSIDE the
# web root, and on a default Apache config https://your-site/.git/config is then
# readable — which exposes the remote URL, and .git/ as a whole is enough to
# reconstruct the full source tree.
#
# Shipping the block here rather than asking each admin to add it by hand means
# it arrives with the update itself, and it survives future updates instead of
# being a local edit that `git pull` fights over.
#
# NOTE for anyone editing this: `<Directory>` and `<DirectoryMatch>` are NOT
# permitted in .htaccess (server-config / virtual-host only) — Apache answers
# 500 for the whole site if you use them here. `RedirectMatch` (mod_alias) and
# `RewriteRule` (mod_rewrite) are both legal in .htaccess, so use those. Two
# mechanisms are kept because a given install may have only one of the modules.
<IfModule mod_alias.c>
    RedirectMatch 404 (^|/)\.git(/|$)
</IfModule>
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
    RewriteEngine On
    RewriteRule (^|/)\.git(/|$) - [F,L]
</IfModule>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Block web access to the directories that are NOT part of the web interface.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. The documented install puts the web root AT the application
# root, so by default every directory in this tree is served. On 2026-07-30 that
# was confirmed from the public internet against a live install:
#
#   GET /backups/<archive>.zip  -> HTTP 200, 110 MB, a full database dump,
#                                  with no authentication at all
#   GET /backups/               -> directory listing of every archive
#   GET /sql/  and  GET /tools/ -> directory listings of 181 and 109 PHP scripts,
#                                  among them sql/run_migrations.php, which
#                                  applies database migrations with no auth
#   GET /inc/db.php             -> served
#
# None of these directories is fetched by the browser. api/, assets/, proxy/,
# sw/, uploads/, cache/ and documentation/ ARE, and must stay reachable —
# proxy/dmr-proxy.php in particular is loaded over HTTP by the radio widget.
#
# THIS FILE IS ONLY HALF THE FIX, and on nginx it is none of it:
#   * nginx NEVER reads .htaccess. An nginx install gets no protection from
#     anything below — it needs the location blocks in docs/nginx/ticketscad-
#     hardening.conf. IIS ignores .htaccess too; sql/web.config + tools/web.config
#     cover the two worst directories there.
#   * Apache reads this file only when the vhost sets AllowOverride FileInfo (or
#     All). On AllowOverride None it is ignored silently.
# So every script under sql/ and tools/ ALSO refuses to run under a web SAPI,
# which is the one defence that works on any server with any configuration, and
# the backup directory has moved above the web root. See docs/WEB-SERVER-
# HARDENING.md.
#
# NOTE for anyone editing this: see the <Directory> warning above — and do NOT
# add `Options -Indexes` here either. `Options` requires AllowOverride Options;
# on a host that grants only FileInfo it makes Apache answer 500 for the WHOLE
# site. Turn indexes off in the vhost instead (the hardening doc shows how); the
# rules below already make the listings for these directories unreachable.
#
# services/ is denied with one deliberate hole: the Mesh Console (Settings →
# Mesh) hands the operator a `curl <this-server>/services/meshtastic/bridge_v2.py`
# command to install the Meshtastic bridge on their radio host, so the bridge
# scripts stay downloadable. Everything else under services/ — listener.ini with
# an APRS-IS passcode, .env files, services/*/logs/ — does not.
#
# THE NAMES BELOW ARE TOP-LEVEL DIRECTORIES, and the patterns must say so.
# The first version of these rules matched `(^|/)…(/|$)`, i.e. the name ANYWHERE
# in the path — so `assets/vendor/` matched the `vendor` entry and every Apache
# install that grants AllowOverride answered 403 for Bootstrap, Leaflet and
# GridStack. The page then rendered unstyled with no map and no widget grid.
# It went unnoticed because the reference deployments run AllowOverride None,
# where this whole file is ignored; XAMPP and most shared hosting do NOT.
# docs/nginx/ticketscad-hardening.conf had it right all along (`location ^~
# /vendor/` is root-anchored), so the two servers had disagreed since 4.2.2.
# `assets/` is fetched by the browser in full and nothing inside it is ever
# denied — hence the allow-list line and the lookbehind.
<IfModule mod_alias.c>
    # RedirectMatch sees the full URL-path (`/newui/assets/vendor/…` on a
    # subdirectory install), so it cannot be anchored with `^`. Excluding the
    # one front-end directory that nests these names is what keeps it honest.
    RedirectMatch 404 (^|/)(?<!assets/)(apache|backups|coordination|drafts|inc|keys|specs|sql|tests|tools|vendor)(/|$)
    RedirectMatch 404 (^|/)services/(?!(meshtastic|meshcore)/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+\.py$)
    RedirectMatch 404 (^|/)\.(env|htpasswd)(/|$)
    RedirectMatch 404 \.(sql|log|bak|old|orig|rej|swp|pem|p8)$
</IfModule>
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
    RewriteEngine On
    # Allow-list first: everything the browser legitimately fetches. In a
    # per-directory context mod_rewrite has already stripped the install's own
    # prefix, so `^assets/` is exactly "the assets directory of this install".
    RewriteRule ^assets/ - [L]
    # The bridge scripts the Mesh Console tells operators to fetch.
    RewriteRule (^|/)services/(meshtastic|meshcore)/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+\.py$ - [L]
    RewriteRule (^|/)(apache|backups|coordination|drafts|inc|keys|services|specs|sql|tests|tools|vendor)(/|$) - [F,L]
    RewriteRule (^|/)\.(env|htpasswd)(/|$) - [F,L]
    RewriteRule \.(sql|log|bak|old|orig|rej|swp|pem|p8)$ - [F,L]
</IfModule>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GHSA-x9x6-w4fg-pmcc — deny cache/zello-audio/ specifically.
#
# Recordings are now written outside the web root (proxy/ZelloProxyApp.php,
# inc/zello_audio_dir.php) and served only via the authenticated
# api/zello-audio.php — this directory should have nothing new land in it.
# The rule stays anyway as defense-in-depth for whatever the relocation
# migration (sql/run_zello_audio_relocate.php) hasn't yet moved, or any file
# that ends up here by some path this fix didn't anticipate.
#
# The match is the full nested path, not the bare "zello-audio" name — the
# lesson from the `vendor` rule above (which matched the name ANYWHERE and
# took out assets/vendor/ with it) is to always anchor on the real location,
# never a directory's own name alone. cache/ itself is untouched: everything
# else under it (weather tiles, zello-images) stays reachable.
<IfModule mod_alias.c>
    RedirectMatch 404 (^|/)cache/zello-audio(/|$)
</IfModule>
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
    RewriteEngine On
    RewriteRule (^|/)cache/zello-audio(/|$) - [F,L]
</IfModule>
